[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"984","stub":{"id":"984","section":"Scotty Brown Bridge to Johnsrud Park","altname":"","river":"Blackfoot River","difficulty":"IItoIII","states":["USA-MNT"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"migration-runnable","latestReading":{"value":"5540","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:30:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":null,"id":"108068","location":{"latitude":"47.018101","longitude":"-113.238998"},"name":"Put In","distance":"0","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"access","description":"This is a common put in for whitewater paddlers seeking the most bang for their buck.","id":"6MkcFwowPEG3sauWW62VD","location":{"latitude":"46.94311154","longitude":"-113.60134126"},"name":"Whittaker Bridge Access Site","distance":"25.63","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"rapid","description":"About two miles below Whitaker Bridge. Class II-III depending on flow, watch for the large rock right-center as the river drops.","id":"102261","location":{"latitude":"46.95324139","longitude":"-113.62063119"},"name":"Thibodeau Rapid","distance":"27.06","difficulty":"III-","approximate":false,"photoID":"0"},{"type":"rapid","description":"A fun surf wave when the water is up in the spring. You can also park and play here using the parking lot directly above and across the road from the wave.","id":"DCS1SZuBftgMakMMGP6Ah","location":{"latitude":"46.91962399","longitude":"-113.67271987"},"name":"The Ledge","distance":"31.31","difficulty":"II","approximate":false,"photoID":null},{"type":"takeout","description":"An often very busy take out.","id":"113311","location":{"latitude":"46.91723011","longitude":"-113.67830488"},"name":"Johnsrud Take Out","distance":"31.54","photoID":"872990","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[{"id":"41050","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"9752","description":"Low water at Round-Up ","caption":"Round-up Rapid","poi_name":"Round-up","subject":"Low water at Round-Up ","author":"Mike Cochran","poi_id":"102261","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/41050","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/41050"}},{"id":"bWL5Qz9cIfwj1iSUuCfZy","ext":"jpg","post_id":"uzd71TyAl1mDyhZC0fVEO","description":"","caption":"Blackfoot at Low Flows","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Ethan Bowen","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2025-09-30T21:05:11.000Z","updated_at":"2025-09-30T21:05:11.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/bWL5Qz9cIfwj1iSUuCfZy","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/bWL5Qz9cIfwj1iSUuCfZy"}},{"id":"872990","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"872991","description":"The Blackfoot attracts a large number of tubers, rafters, swimmers, anglers, and paddlers on hot summer days that drink a large number of canned beverages.  ","caption":"Summer at Johnsrud","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":null,"poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/872990","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/872990"}},{"id":"872988","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"872989","description":"Taking in the scenery on a flat stretch of the Blackfoot River","caption":"Blackfoot Summer","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":null,"poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/872988","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/872988"}},{"id":"7zihgvrhsp9kKrIxeZz5d","ext":"jpg","post_id":"W4OZu9eLtvnhlQWuPHJfg","description":"A nice summer level for a kid trip! ","caption":"Blackfoot fun","poi_name":null,"subject":"Willow Colburn","author":"Kevin Colburn","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2021-07-06T13:44:31.000Z","updated_at":"2021-07-19T13:44:32.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/7zihgvrhsp9kKrIxeZz5d","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/7zihgvrhsp9kKrIxeZz5d"}}],"detail":{"id":"984","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"The Big Blackfoot River is a wonderful river for many types of river enthusiasts.  In the spring the run is a friendly and fun class II/III whitewater run.  Highlights include Thibedeaux Rapids in the middle of the run, and \"The Ledge\" which offers great wave surfing, loops, and even long boat enders depending on the flow.  The Ledge is only in when there is a moderate spring flow.   As summer wears on, the water levels drop, the Blackfoot becomes a tubing mecca for Missoulians seeking to escape the heat, especially from Whitaker Bridge to Bonner.  All the while, the river remains an angling classic, which was immortalized by the book (and movie) A River Runs Through It.\n\nThe river flows through a large valley and is bordered by ponderosa pines, sage, and a healthy riparian shrub community.   Paddlers often see deer, elk, eagles, osprey, beaver, and a large variety of other Montana wildlife.  The river is actively managed by Montana Fish Wildlife and Parks. Montana FWP now maintains boat-in only designated campsites along the Blackfoot.  To reserve a Blackfoot special-use permit, call FWP at (406) 542-5564.  Permits are available for use at the sites beginning June 15.","averageGradient":"15","maxGradient":null,"length":"31.6","correlations":[{"reachID":"984","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"200","beginMediumRunnable":null,"beginHighRunnable":null,"endHighRunnable":"10000"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"Blackfoot River near Bonner MT","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentif